// Go workspace tying the app, its installer operator, and the forge client and
// tenancy rules and admin objects they share, so editor tooling spans them all. Each is its own
// module on purpose:
// controller-runtime's k8s.io/* tree must not constrain the app's KubeVirt/Argo
// client versions, and the operator must not build against the app module.
// The relative replaces in go.mod resolve the pkg modules without the
// workspace, which is how the images build (GOWORK=off) and why ./... at the
// root skips the operator and the pkg modules.
go 1.27.4

use (
	.
	./operator
	./pkg/adminobjects
	./pkg/forge
	./pkg/tenancy
)

// cel-go, which the operator's envtest type-checks the guard with, takes
// genproto's expr API from genproto/googleapis/api; the app's older gnostic
// still requires the monolithic genproto that once carried it too, which a
// workspace build would then find twice. Images build without the workspace.
replace google.golang.org/genproto => google.golang.org/genproto v0.0.0-20261116203732-fd2c7689a808
